---
title: Overview
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

NAHPU is designed to support natural history collections from field collection
through museum curation. The exact workflow depends on each institution's
policies, staff, collection type, and retention requirements.

Use the guideline in this order:

- [Data Curation](./data-curation) to review, normalize, and validate records.
- [Tag Printing](./tag-printing) to prepare specimen tags from reviewed data.
- [Backup and Restore](./backup-restore) to protect databases, project files,
  and user configs.
- [Archiving](./archiving) to preserve project exports and printed documents.

The [Best Practices](../best-practices) section provides broader guidance for
field readiness, project management, data management, and device care.
